Description: USDA 8-digit food codes may contain zero to multiple
    non-duplicated Protein Food (PF) groups, including lean (red) meat,
    lean poultry and cured meat. USDA's Food Patterns Equivalents Databas
    (FPED) and Food Patterns Equivalents Ingredients Databas (FPID) have
    already provided these break-down information. The author's team has
    read through the description and further classify those PF groups into
    subgroups. For example, lean (red) meat is classifed into pork, beef
    and other red meat.
